# E₆ carrier tables: the relations of `I₂ⁿˢ`, the Casimir, the U3 check

Basis: the 78 vectors of `Notes/deligne/audit_2026_10_25/casimir_cert/cert_E6.json` (indices `0..5` Cartan
`H_i`, positive roots `6..41`, negative roots `42..77`).

* `relRaw`: 650 weight vectors spanning `I₂ⁿˢ = V(ω₁+ω₆) ⊂ Sym² 𝔢₆` (the `650`), generated by
  a script not included in this release (exact arithmetic): BFS from the certificate's highest-weight
  vector under the lowering derivations `F_i`, an independent set, integer-scaled.  Lean does not re-check this
  provenance; it uses the relations only as generators.
* `qRaw`: the Casimir `Q` of the certificate.
* `u3OK a c`: the full check of a U3 certificate `c = [L, z x b, …]` for current `a`
  (`L · X_a Q = Σ c · x_c · P_b`), by `E6Sparse.u3Check`.

Data are flat lists of naturals (sign-magnitude integers, `E6Sparse.decZ`).
